# Path claims exempt from verify_claims.py, one glob per line.
#
# This file is repo-local and tracked on purpose. The pre-push hook lives in the
# globally symlinked skills tree, so one copy of it serves every repo that links
# it — a glob written into the hook would silently exempt paths in unrelated
# repos. Globs live here instead, where they show up in a diff and apply to this
# repo only. No file means no globs; nothing is inherited.
#
# Only add a path that is *meant* not to exist here. A path that should exist and
# does not is a defect to fix, not to exempt.

# Ingested sources are intentionally untracked and absent on a fresh clone.
# They are rebuilt from SOURCES.md only when requested.
docs/landing-zone/
docs/landing-zone/**
workstation/cli/*/reference.md
workstation/mcp/*/reference.md

# Paths that exist in a TARGET project, never here. Named individually rather
# than as `.github/**`: this repo owns .github/workflows/verify-docs.yml, and a
# blanket glob exempted that from checking too.
#
# python-quality writes this into a target project from its own template,
# tabulated in that skill's SKILL.md.
.github/workflows/check.yml
#
# Copilot's project-scope instruction and skill locations, documented in
# agent/setup/README.md as what Copilot reads in whichever repo you point it at.
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/skills/**
# Named narrowly: this repo now owns .agents/rules/workbench.md (Antigravity's
# route to AGENTS.md), and `.agents/**` would exempt that from checking too.
.agents/skills/**

# The pre-push hook is installed per clone and is never tracked, so it cannot
# exist on a fresh checkout of any machine. Both references to it are true as
# written — agent/setup/*.md gives the command that creates it, and a machine
# file records whether it is in place. This is the same category the checker
# already exempts for `~/…` paths: machine state, not repo truth.
.git/**

# The root CLAUDE.md is gitignored and written per clone by
# `link_config.py --claude-md --apply`, so a fresh Copilot-only clone has none.
# Docs name it as what Claude Code reads, not as a tracked file.
CLAUDE.md

# drawio-mcp/setup.md quotes upstream's snippet in order to warn against it:
# "Do not follow the README's .claude/settings.json snippet." Documenting a
# thing to avoid does not assert that it exists here.
.claude/**

# The Windows venv interpreter. agent/README.md names it beside .venv/bin/python
# as the second layout the ruff hook's registration probes; a venv has one layout
# or the other, so on any given machine one of the two cannot exist.
.venv/Scripts/python.exe
